185
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:45,981
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's just external.

186
00:13:46,962 --> 00:13:48,643
[SPEAKER_00]: Internal becomes external.

187
00:13:48,963 --> 00:13:50,884
[SPEAKER_00]: Just less external than external-external.

188
00:13:51,985 --> 00:13:56,487
[SPEAKER_00]: Because internal is usually mind, dear, appropriated.

189
00:13:57,708 --> 00:14:01,130
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that internal dimension of putujana stays.

190
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:03,372
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just now seen as external.

191
00:14:04,232 --> 00:14:07,174
[SPEAKER_00]: And things that were external were seen as externally external.

192
00:14:18,008 --> 00:14:31,336
[SPEAKER_01]: Because we're talking about today, about putting the structure of existence into the right order.

193
00:14:32,857 --> 00:14:34,638
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, no, the structure is in the right order.

194
00:14:35,178 --> 00:14:36,479
[SPEAKER_00]: The structure is in the structure.

195
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:44,164
[SPEAKER_00]: You just stop concealing the wrong order on top of the existing order of the structure.

196
00:14:44,484 --> 00:14:45,304
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's doing the same.

197
00:14:45,324 --> 00:14:45,585
[SPEAKER_01]: That's

198
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:50,276
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, in a way, yeah, that means not conceiving, basically.

199
00:14:51,877 --> 00:14:52,918
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the order of things.

200
00:14:53,358 --> 00:14:53,558
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

201
00:14:54,939 --> 00:15:00,402
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, let's, let's put aside the four great elements, because they might be a bit too subtle.

202
00:15:01,102 --> 00:15:04,344
[SPEAKER_00]: But back onto the conscious body, right here.

203
00:15:07,165 --> 00:15:07,726
[SPEAKER_01]: The senses.

204
00:15:07,746 --> 00:15:12,108
[SPEAKER_00]: So you can, as I was telling you today, you can actually touch your eyeball.

205
00:15:13,649 --> 00:15:13,829
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

206
00:15:14,544 --> 00:15:17,786
[SPEAKER_00]: Close your eyelids and you can feel the shape of the planet.

207
00:15:19,247 --> 00:15:25,912
[SPEAKER_00]: And it is that flesh that you're touching, that ball that you're touching with your fingers.

208
00:15:26,152 --> 00:15:38,181
[SPEAKER_00]: That is that because of which there is a whole life of vision, of sights, things you see, desire and lust in regard to them.

209
00:15:38,827 --> 00:15:40,488
[SPEAKER_00]: Fear, in regards to things you see.

210
00:15:40,568 --> 00:15:42,388
[SPEAKER_00]: Grief, in regards to things you see.

211
00:15:42,708 --> 00:15:43,428
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything, basically.

212
00:15:43,448 --> 00:15:45,409
[SPEAKER_00]: The whole world, in regards to things you see.

213
00:15:45,849 --> 00:15:47,190
[SPEAKER_00]: And the same goes for every sense.

214
00:15:48,590 --> 00:15:57,813
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, if you were to touch an apple, that head torch, your eyeball, it's all... it obviously all shares the nature of the matter.

215
00:15:57,833 --> 00:15:58,593
[SPEAKER_00]: It's all material.

216
00:15:59,853 --> 00:16:04,755
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's this particular matter, that pertains to your body, then it's also paired with consciousness.

217
00:16:06,148 --> 00:16:07,889
[SPEAKER_00]: And obviously, you can't see that consciousness.

218
00:16:08,089 --> 00:16:15,271
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just the fact that you can discern that it's purely consciousness because you see as a result of that fleshy eye.

219
00:16:15,291 --> 00:16:19,012
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't see as a result of an apple, or a cup, or a table.

220
00:16:19,452 --> 00:16:20,872
[SPEAKER_00]: You see as a result of this eye.

221
00:16:21,512 --> 00:16:22,613
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the only difference.

222
00:16:24,633 --> 00:16:30,475
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the particular arrangement of that matter enables you to see the forms because the consciousness is there with it.

223
00:16:33,846 --> 00:16:40,830
[SPEAKER_00]: You... there is no further... like, you can't take this to further... to a greater analysis to explain, because, as I said, consciousness doesn't appear.

224
00:16:41,430 --> 00:16:44,331
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can talk about it, but most likely you'll end up conceiving it.

225
00:16:44,451 --> 00:16:48,473
[SPEAKER_00]: You'll end up giving it that which it doesn't have.

226
00:16:49,394 --> 00:16:54,316
[SPEAKER_00]: But what you can do is recognize that it's only the passion in regard to I and forms.

227
00:16:54,857 --> 00:16:56,397
[SPEAKER_00]: Lust in regard to I and forms.

228
00:16:57,158 --> 00:16:58,719
[SPEAKER_00]: Ill will in regard to I and forms.

229
00:16:59,019 --> 00:17:00,539
[SPEAKER_00]: Delusion in regard... That's all it matters.

230
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,600
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what you have to do

231
00:17:02,342 --> 00:17:07,784
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a fun way to regard it, you don't... you stop cultivating... you stop giving possibility for lust to arise in regard to I am forms.

232
00:17:08,665 --> 00:17:09,105
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's it.

233
00:17:10,246 --> 00:17:12,547
[SPEAKER_00]: When that lust is removed, then that's all that needs to be done.

234
00:17:12,567 --> 00:17:22,291
[SPEAKER_00]: Then what is left is this conscious body, this fleshy eye, this fleshy nose, this fleshy tongue, that is still out there below my feet with consciousness.

235
00:17:22,471 --> 00:17:24,672
[SPEAKER_00]: And I know that because things still appear for me.

236
00:17:26,133 --> 00:17:29,214
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, when those aggregates break apart, that's it.

237
00:17:52,474 --> 00:18:04,442
[SPEAKER_01]: We're going to be mindful of the... that which doesn't appear, yet is the basis of your appearance.

238
00:18:05,102 --> 00:18:07,384
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, no, you couldn't be mindful of that which doesn't appear.

239
00:18:08,344 --> 00:18:12,167
[SPEAKER_00]: You can be mindful of the appearance in regard to that because of which appearance is.

240
00:18:13,047 --> 00:18:16,970
[SPEAKER_00]: And the more accurately mindful you are, less conceiving the present.

241
00:18:21,263 --> 00:18:25,146
[SPEAKER_00]: But that which doesn't appear, well, you just made it appear through the statement.

242
00:18:25,246 --> 00:18:26,667
[SPEAKER_00]: It is that which doesn't appear.

243
00:18:28,068 --> 00:18:28,629
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's fine.

244
00:18:28,689 --> 00:18:32,692
[SPEAKER_00]: That's... you... you can't not have a state... you can't not have a designation.

245
00:18:32,732 --> 00:18:35,314
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't not have nāma in regard to rūpa.

246
00:18:35,334 --> 00:18:36,074
[SPEAKER_00]: It's inconceivable.

247
00:18:37,215 --> 00:18:39,517
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what people expect to access rūpa.

248
00:18:40,357 --> 00:18:43,100
[SPEAKER_00]: Or they assume that they have access to rūpa.

249
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,941
[SPEAKER_00]: And then my nāma is kind of optional.

250
00:18:45,581 --> 00:18:46,082
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's not.

251
00:18:46,182 --> 00:18:46,902
[SPEAKER_00]: Nāmarūpa.

252
00:18:47,103 --> 00:18:50,125
[SPEAKER_00]: Rūpa is revealed through the designation of nāma.

253
00:18:50,612 --> 00:18:52,412
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why it's inseparable, nāmarūpa.

254
00:18:54,533 --> 00:18:57,393
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that revelation is very inaccurate.

255
00:18:58,374 --> 00:18:59,134
[SPEAKER_00]: It's conceived.

256
00:19:00,174 --> 00:19:02,915
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all you have to do is sort of make it accurate.

257
00:19:04,435 --> 00:19:05,215
[SPEAKER_00]: Stop conceiving it.

258
00:19:05,395 --> 00:19:05,915
[SPEAKER_00]: Purify it.

259
00:19:07,976 --> 00:19:09,196
[SPEAKER_00]: But all you're going to have is nāmarūpa.

260
00:19:09,976 --> 00:19:13,137
[SPEAKER_00]: As the Buddha said, this conscious body and name and form externally.

261
00:19:13,317 --> 00:19:14,577
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what's left for an arahant.

262
00:19:14,817 --> 00:19:19,778
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even an arahant doesn't remove name in regard to form, or doesn't access form and then name falls off.

263
00:19:21,787 --> 00:19:22,507
[SPEAKER_00]: It's name and form.

264
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:35,409
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just discerning properly, through that name, you can then remove the footing for the form, in terms of conceiving, so you can liberate yourself.

265
00:19:39,250 --> 00:19:42,731
[SPEAKER_00]: So mindfulness in the... let's say mindfulness of the body.

266
00:19:45,291 --> 00:19:51,232
[SPEAKER_00]: And when you think, when you have a thought of mindfulness of the body, you're not actually directly mindful of those four great elements.

267
00:19:52,485 --> 00:19:53,265
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't access them.

268
00:19:53,925 --> 00:19:55,826
[SPEAKER_00]: You're mindful of their appearance.

269
00:19:56,626 --> 00:19:58,527
[SPEAKER_00]: Or rather, you're mindful of appearance.

270
00:19:59,247 --> 00:20:00,327
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's what appearance is.

271
00:20:00,467 --> 00:20:01,327
[SPEAKER_00]: Not their appearance.

272
00:20:01,387 --> 00:20:02,047
[SPEAKER_00]: The appearance is.

273
00:20:02,387 --> 00:20:04,888
[SPEAKER_00]: And the appearance is because the four great elements are still there, standing.

274
00:20:05,328 --> 00:20:10,009
[SPEAKER_01]: Is that the body that should be noticed in satipaṭṭhāna?

275
00:20:10,449 --> 00:20:10,690
[SPEAKER_01]: That's...

276
00:20:11,370 --> 00:20:11,610
[SPEAKER_01]: Which?

277
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:12,270
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you mean by that?

278
00:20:12,290 --> 00:20:13,450
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's what you've got to understand.

279
00:20:13,470 --> 00:20:18,691
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what body that you're seeing, being mindful of, is the body that appeared.

280
00:20:20,032 --> 00:20:20,332
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

281
00:20:21,206 --> 00:20:24,247
[SPEAKER_00]: If you're properly mindful, you will understand mindfulness.

282
00:20:24,287 --> 00:20:25,388
[SPEAKER_00]: You will understand appearance.

283
00:20:25,948 --> 00:20:27,088
[SPEAKER_00]: You would stop conceiving.

284
00:20:29,929 --> 00:20:33,931
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you, even through the practice of mindfulness, still think, no, this is that body.

285
00:20:34,531 --> 00:20:36,472
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's comprised of the four great elements.

286
00:20:36,632 --> 00:20:40,634
[SPEAKER_00]: It means the appearance is made of it, but that's all you have.

287
00:20:40,874 --> 00:20:46,636
[SPEAKER_00]: But the mindfulness, if you start being mindful correctly, it's not mine, not for me, not I am.

288
00:20:48,008 --> 00:20:48,709
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's it.

289
00:20:48,829 --> 00:21:00,298
[SPEAKER_00]: As I said, you can't be mindful of the actual elements behind the body, or underneath it, but you can disown the body, which then will become an accurate representation of the four great elements.

290
00:21:00,338 --> 00:21:03,200
[SPEAKER_00]: And their ultimate nature is, they are not yours.

291
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,281
[SPEAKER_00]: They cannot be yours.

292
00:21:04,541 --> 00:21:06,963
[SPEAKER_00]: They can... they... they're not even possible to be yours.

293
00:21:07,724 --> 00:21:16,011
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you start emulating that in regard to appearance, and eventually, it will... it will stand for... for how things actually are, which means you've been around.

294
00:21:16,371 --> 00:21:17,412
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you can't undo it.

295
00:21:18,763 --> 00:21:22,625
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's proper mindfulness has to be paired with that knowledge.

296
00:21:23,725 --> 00:21:24,265
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely.

297
00:21:24,285 --> 00:21:26,146
[SPEAKER_00]: Right view comes first.

298
00:21:27,847 --> 00:21:32,869
[SPEAKER_00]: Even the mindfulness cannot be the right one, if there's no right view, no matter how general that mindfulness is.

299
00:21:34,869 --> 00:21:42,933
[SPEAKER_00]: The right view always comes first, which is why you have to... and it makes everything else right, done, done upon it.

300
00:21:52,743 --> 00:21:53,704
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like this, eh...

301
00:21:55,445 --> 00:22:04,690
[SPEAKER_01]: In the Ānāpānasati Sutta, there's a one section in the beginning, it says, calming... it's always translated, calming the bodily formation.

302
00:22:05,630 --> 00:22:06,931
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the bodily formation?

303
00:22:08,092 --> 00:22:09,452
[SPEAKER_01]: The breath, breathing.

304
00:22:13,215 --> 00:22:16,376
[SPEAKER_00]: Ānāpānasati Sutta, Kāyā-saṃphara, yeah.

305
00:22:16,416 --> 00:22:17,137
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

306
00:22:18,507 --> 00:22:28,795
[SPEAKER_01]: He, while breathing in, he experiences the whole body, or the whole breath, that people say the breath of body, but he experiences while he's breathing, the whole body.

307
00:22:29,535 --> 00:22:39,222
[SPEAKER_01]: And then the next, next sentence says, like, while breathing, yeah, he breathes calming the body formation.

308
00:22:40,043 --> 00:22:47,208
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, if the body formation is breathing, he's just, he couldn't have said calming the breath.

309
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:53,321
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, then, he could have said that, but then it wouldn't serve... it wouldn't be seen as saṅkhara.

310
00:22:53,781 --> 00:23:01,262
[SPEAKER_00]: It wouldn't serve for the recognition and cultivation of the simultaneous principle of saṅkhara and sankhārta-dharmak.

311
00:23:01,662 --> 00:23:02,422
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the whole point.

312
00:23:03,063 --> 00:23:05,063
[SPEAKER_00]: Full understanding of the principle means arahanty.

313
00:23:06,503 --> 00:23:11,684
[SPEAKER_00]: But if he just said, just calm your breath, you won't be seeing body dependent upon the action of breathing.

314
00:23:13,604 --> 00:23:14,605
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, this...

315
00:23:14,805 --> 00:23:16,565
[SPEAKER_00]: I think... And the point... the point with that sentence

316
00:23:18,792 --> 00:23:21,153
[SPEAKER_00]: You take on mindfully an act of breathing.

317
00:23:21,713 --> 00:23:24,613
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same sense, eh... what is it?

318
00:23:25,314 --> 00:23:26,794
[SPEAKER_00]: The turner, the wheel turner.

319
00:23:27,434 --> 00:23:29,415
[SPEAKER_00]: Turns the wheel like this, turns the wheel like that.

320
00:23:29,475 --> 00:23:30,835
[SPEAKER_00]: You breathe in like this, you breathe...

321
00:23:30,855 --> 00:23:37,937
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not that you're trying to control it, in terms of, eh... stop it or force it.

322
00:23:38,677 --> 00:23:46,359
[SPEAKER_00]: The breathing is there, but you kind of... like, imagine the horses that are already running, but then you join in and you take the reins.

323
00:23:46,883 --> 00:23:49,446
[SPEAKER_00]: But you don't interfere with their running, but you do take their aims.

324
00:23:50,527 --> 00:23:54,011
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you might slow it down or something, but they still go in the direction and you're not changing that.

325
00:23:54,993 --> 00:23:58,236
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you take on, mindfully, the act of breathing.

326
00:23:58,377 --> 00:24:03,623
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, and then you can influence, through the existing act of breathing, you can, okay, prolong the breath, shorten the breath.

327
00:24:04,163 --> 00:24:06,186
[SPEAKER_00]: The point is, you're mindful of the breathing.

328
00:24:07,530 --> 00:24:11,112
[SPEAKER_00]: That experience, being mindful of the breathing, because breathing is bodily.

329
00:24:11,353 --> 00:24:12,273
[SPEAKER_00]: It's bound with the body.

330
00:24:12,553 --> 00:24:13,334
[SPEAKER_00]: It's inseparable.

331
00:24:13,354 --> 00:24:14,395
[SPEAKER_00]: It's inconceivable.

332
00:24:14,815 --> 00:24:19,298
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even just the thought of breathing already implies the experience of the body.

333
00:24:19,338 --> 00:24:19,898
[SPEAKER_00]: It's in there.

334
00:24:20,879 --> 00:24:27,063
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you're thinking about breathing, when you're breathing, through that, you're already implying a form of experience of the body.

335
00:24:27,083 --> 00:24:30,185
[SPEAKER_00]: And that experience of the body is determined by your active engagement in breathing.

336
00:24:30,878 --> 00:24:34,539
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you recognize it because the breathing, the body is there and obviously body is bound with the breathing.

337
00:24:35,119 --> 00:24:41,321
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't mean that... it doesn't necessarily mean cause and effect, like breathing results in body.

338
00:24:42,062 --> 00:24:42,142
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

339
00:24:42,162 --> 00:24:43,602
[SPEAKER_00]: It means they're inseparable.

340
00:24:43,642 --> 00:24:43,922
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

341
00:24:43,942 --> 00:24:44,462
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all it means.

342
00:24:44,502 --> 00:24:46,503
[SPEAKER_00]: They always occur together, never apart.

343
00:24:46,863 --> 00:24:48,444
[SPEAKER_00]: Inconceivable to have them apart.

344
00:24:51,164 --> 00:24:55,086
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't conceive the breathing without a body implied in that act.

345
00:24:55,306 --> 00:24:55,886
[SPEAKER_00]: You just can't.

346
00:24:57,272 --> 00:25:02,774
[SPEAKER_00]: No matter, even if it's the utmost abstraction, if you think breathing, it implies the body.

347
00:25:03,514 --> 00:25:06,655
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, in the time, it's... it's a body with... it's a body with saṅkhāra.

348
00:25:06,955 --> 00:25:08,196
[SPEAKER_00]: It's bound up with the body.

349
00:25:10,076 --> 00:25:17,739
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then you recognize, okay, because this is inseparable from... this experience of the body, right here, now, separate from breathing.

350
00:25:17,819 --> 00:25:19,439
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't have to think about your act of breathing.

351
00:25:19,979 --> 00:25:24,521
[SPEAKER_00]: But this body here, it's that body that is inseparable from breathing.

352
00:25:25,827 --> 00:25:31,570
[SPEAKER_00]: So, any form of experience of the body, it will be the body that implies breathing, inasmuch breathing implies the body.

353
00:25:33,791 --> 00:25:41,855
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, through calming down the mindful act of breathing... Oh, no!

354
00:25:42,215 --> 00:25:54,361
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that body, that abstract body, you can say even like that, that is implied in my thought of breathing, that abstract body is this body right here, right there, and their relationship is external.

355
00:25:56,601 --> 00:26:03,503
[SPEAKER_00]: But that body that you think of, when you look through the act of breathing, is that body right here, right now.

356
00:26:04,884 --> 00:26:19,649
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, through affecting, through calming down the act of breathing, calming down those thoughts in regard to the act of breathing, actually, you are pertaining, you are gradually affecting the body right here, right now.

357
00:26:20,869 --> 00:26:22,610
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that relationship is external.

358
00:26:23,090 --> 00:26:25,951
[SPEAKER_00]: The thoughts that you have in regard to breathing and the body,

359
00:26:27,027 --> 00:26:28,368
[SPEAKER_00]: That's assumed in that breathing.

360
00:26:28,508 --> 00:26:29,269
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not in your head.

361
00:26:29,409 --> 00:26:31,230
[SPEAKER_00]: That thought is the appearance of a thing.

362
00:26:33,131 --> 00:26:45,099
[SPEAKER_00]: And that thought, that thought that has the tacit implication of a body in regard to breathing, that body there is the body that's right here, right there, right now, sorry.

363
00:26:48,001 --> 00:26:55,286
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you think breathing and that abstract body that appears, that body is the body that you can access through your body.

364
00:26:56,223 --> 00:26:57,824
[SPEAKER_00]: Not necessarily through the thoughts of breathing.

365
00:26:59,044 --> 00:26:59,505
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's it.

366
00:26:59,825 --> 00:27:02,686
[SPEAKER_00]: It's this conscious body and name and form externally.

367
00:27:03,727 --> 00:27:09,490
[SPEAKER_00]: The thoughts of breathing are the name and forms externally that imply that body, this conscious body right here, right now.

368
00:27:10,810 --> 00:27:20,255
[SPEAKER_00]: So, instead of maintaining the the the connection of my body, my thoughts, you actually pull it out and you recognize, no, it's the conscious body right here, right now.

369
00:27:20,295 --> 00:27:23,657
[SPEAKER_00]: And when I think about it, that's also externally in regard to the conscious body.

370
00:27:23,677 --> 00:27:25,618
[SPEAKER_00]: There is no internal dimension that is mine.

371
00:27:28,033 --> 00:27:43,936
[SPEAKER_00]: So, through cultivating the act of breathing, the thoughts of breathing, the mindfulness of breathing, you start discerning a phenomenon of body within that act of breathing, that is actually this body right here, right now, just seen from a different view at the same time.

372
00:27:46,497 --> 00:27:47,317
[SPEAKER_01]: The body that appears.

373
00:27:47,957 --> 00:27:48,237
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

374
00:27:50,398 --> 00:27:52,078
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, don't, don't, yeah, don't worry.

375
00:27:52,098 --> 00:27:52,998
[SPEAKER_00]: That's a different approach.

376
00:27:53,138 --> 00:27:57,519
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't, don't try and mix it, the elements and that because of which it appears.

377
00:28:00,582 --> 00:28:09,144
[SPEAKER_00]: But yeah, if you start seeing it at the same time, if a thing is present twice or seen at the same time from two points of view, so to speak, none of them can be yours.

378
00:28:09,785 --> 00:28:12,885
[SPEAKER_00]: Because mine, me, I am, requires that singularity.

379
00:28:13,185 --> 00:28:14,646
[SPEAKER_00]: I look from here towards there.

380
00:28:15,366 --> 00:28:21,928
[SPEAKER_00]: But now you recognize the thing is present, seen from there, and experienced right here, at the same time, which one is yours?

381
00:28:23,848 --> 00:28:25,929
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you realize none of them can be yours.

382
00:28:37,056 --> 00:29:00,981
[SPEAKER_00]: So, put your attention on the experience of the body right here, right now, and then start breathing, and through that breathing, discern the body, that then you start basically, right, discerning as, oh, the body that I'm, this, this, this abstract phenomenon of the body that I'm discerning through my breathing, actually stands for this very body that I'm experiencing right here, right now.

383
00:29:01,642 --> 00:29:03,662
[SPEAKER_00]: But their relationship is external.

384
00:29:16,663 --> 00:29:19,485
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you can spread it with a thought of the body.

385
00:29:19,965 --> 00:29:21,086
[SPEAKER_00]: That's already nāmarūpa.

386
00:29:22,607 --> 00:29:28,211
[SPEAKER_00]: That then you just conceive to be, oh, this is this body right here, right now, through that internal connection.

387
00:29:29,893 --> 00:29:35,977
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, my thought is this body, comes from this body, it's this body, in the body, out of the body, from the body, it's for me, it's mine.

388
00:29:39,420 --> 00:29:45,444
[SPEAKER_00]: But when you recognize the thought of the body as an arisen phenomenon externally,

389
00:29:48,487 --> 00:29:50,509
[SPEAKER_00]: And then see it standing for that body out there.

390
00:29:58,835 --> 00:30:00,336
[SPEAKER_01]: For that body out there?

391
00:30:00,356 --> 00:30:00,597
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

392
00:30:01,577 --> 00:30:01,938
[SPEAKER_01]: Out where?

393
00:30:01,978 --> 00:30:02,378
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you mean?

394
00:30:02,638 --> 00:30:03,118
[SPEAKER_00]: Out where?

395
00:30:03,279 --> 00:30:04,239
[SPEAKER_00]: Out there, right here.

396
00:30:07,442 --> 00:30:10,905
[SPEAKER_00]: For that fleshy eye, for that nose, for the tongue.

397
00:30:11,885 --> 00:30:14,988
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, fleshy eye, it's a designation, it's an appearance.

398
00:30:16,105 --> 00:30:17,346
[SPEAKER_00]: That stands for the fleshly eye.

399
00:30:17,846 --> 00:30:20,507
[SPEAKER_00]: But you assume, oh, it's my fleshly eye.

400
00:30:21,968 --> 00:30:32,012
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you see that that fleshly eye will not be known, if there is no external appearance of a thought, fleshly eye, phenomena, without, it's just inconceivable, inseparable from.

401
00:30:33,253 --> 00:30:34,213
[SPEAKER_00]: Then it can't be yours.

402
00:30:34,673 --> 00:30:35,974
[SPEAKER_00]: Then it just becomes all external.

403
00:30:36,454 --> 00:30:39,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, it's all out there, just there, right here, or yonder, whatever.

404
00:30:39,476 --> 00:30:40,176
[SPEAKER_00]: None of it is mine.

405
00:30:45,687 --> 00:30:46,327
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's the thing.

406
00:30:46,347 --> 00:30:54,732
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to keep constantly attending to this body right here, right now, because this body is right here, right now, and you have no choice about it.

407
00:30:54,752 --> 00:31:03,858
[SPEAKER_00]: All you want to do is stop misconceiving it, or misconceiving things that appear in regard to this body right here, right now.

408
00:31:05,218 --> 00:31:13,223
[SPEAKER_00]: So, mindfulness of breathing, through actively engaging in an act of breathing, you start discerning the body, the phenomenal body.

409
00:31:14,492 --> 00:31:17,915
[SPEAKER_00]: Which then you can go, this is my body, this is the same as this body, this is the body.

410
00:31:18,315 --> 00:31:24,420
[SPEAKER_00]: Or you can start seeing this body, it's basically that representation that we spoke earlier, of the body present right here, right now.

411
00:31:25,341 --> 00:31:26,622
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's one way of looking at it.

412
00:31:27,163 --> 00:31:31,186
[SPEAKER_00]: Or you can then just be mindful of the present body, conscious body, right here, right now.

413
00:31:38,992 --> 00:31:39,613
[SPEAKER_00]: In many... well,

414
00:31:40,362 --> 00:31:43,884
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't really imagine it, because if you would imagine it accurately, it wouldn't be imagination.

415
00:31:43,904 --> 00:31:46,485
[SPEAKER_00]: It would stand for how things are.

416
00:31:48,246 --> 00:31:51,708
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever arises is seen from two points of view.

417
00:31:52,949 --> 00:31:53,229
[SPEAKER_00]: Always.

418
00:31:53,569 --> 00:31:54,850
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't just have one point of view.

419
00:31:55,870 --> 00:31:56,491
[SPEAKER_00]: Inconceivable.

420
00:32:00,253 --> 00:32:02,634
[SPEAKER_00]: So it's always present.

421
00:32:04,895 --> 00:32:05,175
[SPEAKER_00]: Twice.

422
00:32:05,696 --> 00:32:06,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Simultaneous.

423
00:32:06,516 --> 00:32:06,976
[SPEAKER_00]: Not twice.

424
00:32:07,016 --> 00:32:07,857
[SPEAKER_00]: There will be one, too.

425
00:32:09,217 --> 00:32:10,818
[SPEAKER_00]: As a presence, it's double.

426
00:32:22,008 --> 00:32:23,169
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, explain that.

427
00:32:24,270 --> 00:32:24,570
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

428
00:32:27,072 --> 00:32:28,113
[SPEAKER_00]: I can try, but I can't.

429
00:32:28,173 --> 00:32:28,833
[SPEAKER_00]: I can see that.

430
00:32:30,535 --> 00:32:33,037
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, everything's seen from two different points of view.

431
00:32:33,077 --> 00:32:34,838
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, no, like everything already is.

432
00:32:35,459 --> 00:32:36,219
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

433
00:32:36,279 --> 00:32:36,760
[SPEAKER_00]: It arises.

434
00:32:39,424 --> 00:32:48,090
[SPEAKER_00]: There are two points of view to every experience, simultaneously present, which is why you can then develop the assumption of one point of view, which is me.

435
00:32:59,818 --> 00:33:02,580
[SPEAKER_00]: If you were to see that you're the center of your sense of self,

436
00:33:04,830 --> 00:33:07,431
[SPEAKER_00]: It's always determined by something else different than that sense of self.

437
00:33:07,611 --> 00:33:08,552
[SPEAKER_00]: It's two things at present.

438
00:33:09,092 --> 00:33:11,473
[SPEAKER_00]: The central sense of self and that which determines it.

439
00:33:14,414 --> 00:33:15,095
[SPEAKER_00]: At the same time.

440
00:33:15,755 --> 00:33:16,875
[SPEAKER_00]: It's simultaneously present.

441
00:33:16,996 --> 00:33:17,536
[SPEAKER_00]: Akālika.

442
00:33:17,876 --> 00:33:18,536
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what it means.

443
00:33:18,736 --> 00:33:19,737
[SPEAKER_00]: Not pertaining to time.

444
00:33:21,478 --> 00:33:22,258
[SPEAKER_00]: It's simultaneous.

445
00:33:22,318 --> 00:33:23,498
[SPEAKER_00]: There is no time in between.

446
00:33:29,581 --> 00:33:33,523
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whichever point of view you took to be yours, within that you discern

447
00:33:34,742 --> 00:33:44,828
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, no matter what point of view you take to be yours, simultaneously to that, it's determined by that which cannot be yours at the same time.

448
00:33:45,569 --> 00:33:53,073
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you can't have both things at the same time, because that would require a third point of view, that's more general to these two points, but that's inconceivable.

449
00:33:55,334 --> 00:33:56,855
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can't help but have a point of view

450
00:33:57,558 --> 00:34:07,723
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, sorry, you can't help but attend one point of view, but through that you discern another direction, that it's not the same direction, that it determines this direction.

451
00:34:10,985 --> 00:34:15,827
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there is a direction of the conscious body, and there is a direction of the name and form externally.

452
00:34:17,588 --> 00:34:22,210
[SPEAKER_00]: And you can discern both of them simultaneously present.

453
00:34:22,270 --> 00:34:25,252
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, you will have to be attending one on account of the other.

454
00:34:25,858 --> 00:34:28,920
[SPEAKER_00]: If you attend conscious body, you'll be discerning never-forming standard.

455
00:34:29,720 --> 00:34:32,641
[SPEAKER_00]: If you attend never-forming standard, you'll be discerning conscious body through that.

456
00:34:34,342 --> 00:34:44,107
[SPEAKER_00]: But if that's all you can ever have, if you contemplate it long enough, you'll stop assuming one single unifying point of view, that it's neither here nor there, nor both, nor whatever.

457
00:34:44,787 --> 00:34:47,249
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's only maintained through a simple not.

458
00:34:47,989 --> 00:34:50,050
[SPEAKER_00]: Not discerning of the arrangement of things.

459
00:34:50,970 --> 00:34:54,132
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, by not fully understanding that things cannot be yours,

460
00:34:54,812 --> 00:34:56,893
[SPEAKER_00]: You maintain the notion of their mind.

461
00:35:00,756 --> 00:35:07,361
[SPEAKER_00]: So, right here, right now, while you're thinking about what I've just said, your body is seated present with the conscious and spared with it.

462
00:35:09,382 --> 00:35:10,623
[SPEAKER_00]: Those are two simultaneous things.

463
00:35:12,524 --> 00:35:22,571
[SPEAKER_00]: And no matter how hard you're thinking, whatever you're thinking, through that, the discernment of this conscious body present right here, right now, is possible.

464
00:35:22,952 --> 00:35:23,272
[SPEAKER_00]: Because

465
00:35:23,672 --> 00:35:25,293
[SPEAKER_00]: This conscious body right here is there.

466
00:35:26,653 --> 00:35:30,934
[SPEAKER_00]: And in this particular instance, it's basically the reason why you're able to think in the first place.

467
00:35:34,635 --> 00:35:36,916
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why any dhamma can also be a saṅkhara.

468
00:35:36,996 --> 00:35:40,077
[SPEAKER_00]: Any of the aggregates can also be a determination.

469
00:35:42,498 --> 00:35:43,838
[SPEAKER_01]: As we say, watching the breath.

470
00:35:44,318 --> 00:35:46,659
[SPEAKER_00]: It depends what you attend, then the opposite.

471
00:35:46,699 --> 00:35:48,780
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to discern the opposite of where your attention is.

472
00:35:50,182 --> 00:35:51,543
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if I'm watching the body...

473
00:35:51,563 --> 00:35:52,484
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you're watching the body...

474
00:35:52,684 --> 00:35:56,066
[SPEAKER_01]: I can see that it's been... the termination is the breath.

475
00:35:56,886 --> 00:35:58,187
[SPEAKER_01]: But I'm not looking at the breath, are I?

476
00:35:58,207 --> 00:36:01,670
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess so, yeah.

477
00:36:01,810 --> 00:36:02,990
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

478
00:36:03,891 --> 00:36:05,112
[SPEAKER_01]: I can see it in the background.

479
00:36:06,613 --> 00:36:08,654
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, if I'm looking at the breath, I can see the body...

480
00:36:08,834 --> 00:36:09,955
[SPEAKER_00]: In the practice of ānāpānasati.

481
00:36:10,455 --> 00:36:10,956
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

482
00:36:10,996 --> 00:36:11,896
[SPEAKER_01]: So...

483
00:36:15,218 --> 00:36:17,500
[SPEAKER_01]: But just in terms of that practice...

484
00:36:18,942 --> 00:36:25,366
[SPEAKER_00]: Watching the breath and having... Well, in terms of that practice, yeah, you want to be, you want to be doing mindfulness of breathing.

485
00:36:25,406 --> 00:36:31,709
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to be actively, because it's a form of an act, that you want to tune yourself into.

486
00:36:34,731 --> 00:36:35,111
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

487
00:36:35,871 --> 00:36:36,692
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you're breathing.

488
00:36:37,572 --> 00:36:46,297
[SPEAKER_00]: And you recognize, through this very act, you start discerning the implicit notion of the body, present right there, right then.

489
00:36:48,154 --> 00:37:15,749
[SPEAKER_00]: If something were to happen while you're breathing there and discerning that body through that body, if those elements that that body is comprised of would change, disappear, be affected by some other external factor, you realize that all acts

490
00:37:16,137 --> 00:37:20,558
[SPEAKER_00]: That you're still mindfully engaging your breathing, cannot remain standing.

491
00:37:21,998 --> 00:37:25,319
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, its foundations are completely inaccessible to you.

492
00:37:27,219 --> 00:37:27,899
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't have it.

493
00:37:29,180 --> 00:37:33,681
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if something happens to grey elements, you can't possibly continue breathing.

494
00:37:33,701 --> 00:37:36,521
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't possibly continue discerning the body through that.

495
00:37:38,582 --> 00:37:45,463
[SPEAKER_00]: So, through contemplating like that, you have abandoned the very nature of action, of intentional action.

496
00:37:46,721 --> 00:37:48,702
[SPEAKER_00]: It's an act.

497
00:37:49,262 --> 00:37:51,064
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a neutral act, which is why we praise it.

498
00:37:53,506 --> 00:38:01,732
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you cultivate it long enough, you develop mindfulness that then won't be disturbed by any other form of act that are not unwholesome.

499
00:38:01,772 --> 00:38:03,413
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, they have to be abandoned beforehand.

500
00:38:04,694 --> 00:38:11,800
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you're sitting, walking, eating, talking, none of it then becomes... well, none of them... none of that continues to imply

501
00:38:14,173 --> 00:38:17,134
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, the notion of permanence, the notion of control in regard to things.

502
00:38:19,135 --> 00:38:21,916
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you abandon your own intention, it ceases to be yours.

503
00:38:22,977 --> 00:38:38,443
[SPEAKER_00]: Because through practicing of intentional attending to breathing, and breathing in like this, breathing out like that, discerning the body through that, and then seeing that if that thing changes, if that determination is swept away, none of your present acts can remain.

504
00:38:39,084 --> 00:38:40,024
[SPEAKER_00]: You do that long enough,

505
00:38:40,558 --> 00:38:46,400
[SPEAKER_00]: None of the notions of I am, and this is me, this is for me, can remain standing.

506
00:38:46,480 --> 00:38:47,501
[SPEAKER_00]: It will just evaporate.

507
00:38:50,362 --> 00:38:54,623
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you just breathe, and through breathing, simultaneously, you discern the presence of the body.

508
00:38:55,564 --> 00:39:00,345
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, you can start attending to the body right here, right now, but then, obviously, you're not mindful of the breathing anymore.

509
00:39:01,666 --> 00:39:02,126
[SPEAKER_00]: It's fine.

510
00:39:02,186 --> 00:39:04,767
[SPEAKER_00]: You can be mindful of the body, but then, you're not doing ānāpānasati.

511
00:39:04,787 --> 00:39:05,527
[SPEAKER_00]: That's also fine.

512
00:39:06,028 --> 00:39:09,469
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, it's just one wave of developing mindfulness.

513
00:39:10,755 --> 00:39:14,816
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you want to stick to ānāpānasati, you just continue breathing in while you're descending body through that.

514
00:39:15,376 --> 00:39:20,817
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you realize, oh, if I... if I calm down this breathing, this active engagement, that body will calm down.

515
00:39:25,278 --> 00:39:32,980
[SPEAKER_00]: If I slow it down, the experience of that body through that slowing down of breath will be affected as well.

516
00:39:34,461 --> 00:39:40,262
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you can contemplate the four noble truths or any other thing, as the Buddha says, through that breathing.

517
00:39:40,968 --> 00:39:49,772
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you have refined your active engagement with the action, with the nature of action.

518
00:39:50,473 --> 00:39:55,135
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you're not distracted, you're doing it mindfully, and through that you're discerning the present.

519
00:39:55,335 --> 00:40:02,499
[SPEAKER_00]: Because no matter what you're doing, whether you're sweeping leaves, walking, sitting, talking, there is an implication to your body present right there, right there, simultaneously.

520
00:40:03,039 --> 00:40:09,002
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if that body is not present right there, right then, simultaneously, you wouldn't be able to be engaging in these acts actively at the very time.

521
00:40:11,556 --> 00:40:13,217
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just that you don't... you're not aware of it.

522
00:40:13,317 --> 00:40:21,882
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not aware of the presence of the body, while you engage actively in this task, because your attention is unmindful.

523
00:40:23,923 --> 00:40:26,685
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, you maintain the notion of procreation through that very thing.

524
00:40:27,445 --> 00:40:34,209
[SPEAKER_00]: But you start discerning the body, and then you recognize that, well, there is no room for me and I am, in that act.

525
00:40:34,910 --> 00:40:40,233
[SPEAKER_00]: That act, this act, these intentions, these choices I'm making, next moment,

526
00:40:41,330 --> 00:40:52,300
[SPEAKER_00]: These are all possible because there is this... well, there is the implication you can see through of the body right while those acts are present.

527
00:40:54,382 --> 00:41:01,248
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's that thought that is crystallizing of that body that's revealed through

528
00:41:01,732 --> 00:41:03,192
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindful engagement with these acts.

529
00:41:03,372 --> 00:41:05,433
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, the body is always present.

530
00:41:05,553 --> 00:41:07,913
[SPEAKER_00]: There's a phenomenon of present body through these acts.

531
00:41:08,413 --> 00:41:12,494
[SPEAKER_00]: And that body is that which this body is, when I think about it, separate.

532
00:41:13,414 --> 00:41:17,075
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whether you think about the body directly or indirectly, you stop conceiving it as yours.

533
00:41:17,595 --> 00:41:20,956
[SPEAKER_00]: You see it as that thing out there, because of which you're able to move and act and choose.

534
00:41:21,536 --> 00:41:28,437
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you start seeing your own choices as a result, because of that present conscious body out there, right there, at the time.

535
00:41:31,020 --> 00:41:42,710
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, next time you make a choice, or rather, when you have practiced this efficiently, then when the choices are being made, even that, the most personal thing, I want this over that, ceases to induce the notion of personality.

536
00:41:44,251 --> 00:41:46,413
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's understanding, it's seeing through and through.

537
00:41:50,576 --> 00:41:53,959
[SPEAKER_00]: Would you be able to think unrelated things to your body?

538
00:41:54,199 --> 00:41:57,622
[SPEAKER_00]: Just think something completely out of the imagination?

539
00:41:58,890 --> 00:42:04,953
[SPEAKER_00]: So, no matter how disconnected, unrelated your thoughts might be, the nature of the thought is bound with the body.

540
00:42:05,013 --> 00:42:06,234
[SPEAKER_00]: In as much, the body is bound with the mind, i.e.

541
00:42:06,254 --> 00:42:06,454
[SPEAKER_00]: thoughts.

542
00:42:24,467 --> 00:42:27,311
[SPEAKER_00]: Hence, it only depends what you attend, it will be determined by the other.

543
00:42:27,791 --> 00:42:41,670
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you wouldn't be able to even think about body, talk about body, if the mind doesn't designate it at the time as body, as that, as that physical in regard to itself, or that less mental in regard to itself.

544
00:42:45,662 --> 00:42:53,127
[SPEAKER_00]: So, before you're saying that, those thoughts in regard to body would stop conceiving, would stop making you assume that that is actually that matter.

545
00:42:53,427 --> 00:42:53,607
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

546
00:42:53,747 --> 00:42:54,528
[SPEAKER_00]: It's still thoughts.

547
00:42:55,509 --> 00:42:57,370
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all you can have is thoughts and thoughts.

548
00:42:57,830 --> 00:42:59,131
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why the mind comes first.

549
00:43:02,193 --> 00:43:03,494
[SPEAKER_00]: Would you know a cup as a cup?

550
00:43:04,615 --> 00:43:07,136
[SPEAKER_00]: Would you know matter as matter?

551
00:43:07,376 --> 00:43:09,778
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, even saying it matter, thinking it matter.

552
00:43:10,679 --> 00:43:12,520
[SPEAKER_00]: That's already a designation.

553
00:43:12,540 --> 00:43:13,160
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all you have.

554
00:43:14,161 --> 00:43:14,341
[SPEAKER_00]: Just

555
00:43:14,957 --> 00:43:18,139
[SPEAKER_00]: Designations are different levels of generality, pertaining to different things.

556
00:43:19,440 --> 00:43:20,341
[SPEAKER_00]: What's the designation?

557
00:43:54,315 --> 00:44:10,226
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what you want to do is make sure that when it comes to designation of the body, in regard to body, whether peripherally, whether directly, when you're attending it, you don't conceive that that is that matter.

558
00:44:10,666 --> 00:44:13,508
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't conceive that that is what those great elements are.

559
00:44:15,349 --> 00:44:16,850
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it will always remain below your feet.

560
00:44:18,551 --> 00:44:21,713
[SPEAKER_00]: There will always remain that because of which this appearance is.

561
00:44:22,973 --> 00:44:25,975
[SPEAKER_00]: And this appearance, in this case, is the designation of this body.

562
00:44:26,335 --> 00:44:27,556
[SPEAKER_00]: Right here, right now, that I'm seeing.

563
00:44:27,916 --> 00:44:28,957
[SPEAKER_00]: I can touch parts of it.

564
00:44:30,237 --> 00:44:31,218
[SPEAKER_00]: I can think about it.

565
00:44:32,098 --> 00:44:32,699
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all fine.

566
00:44:33,559 --> 00:44:35,160
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the only thing you can have.

567
00:44:35,780 --> 00:44:37,161
[SPEAKER_00]: Even in terms of if you think about it.

568
00:44:37,982 --> 00:44:42,164
[SPEAKER_00]: Just stop conceiving that to be standing for this external world of four varied elements.

569
00:44:42,524 --> 00:44:43,645
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's another thought.

570
00:44:47,665 --> 00:44:51,489
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what you have is thoughts in regards to thoughts, but those thoughts can be discerned.

571
00:44:51,609 --> 00:44:59,997
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, they are because of the four great elements that I'm thinking right here, right now, which is all I can do, but I'm not conceiving to be those four great elements.

572
00:45:00,818 --> 00:45:01,739
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the important thing.

573
00:45:01,939 --> 00:45:08,706
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if you only say, oh, all you have is your thoughts, then you, well, you'll fall into a very obvious, naive form of idealism.

574
00:45:08,766 --> 00:45:10,388
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, whatever you think it's in your head.

575
00:45:10,428 --> 00:45:10,748
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, no.

576
00:45:11,445 --> 00:45:15,868
[SPEAKER_00]: See, whenever I think it's in my head, you assume your head to be material in regard to your thoughts.

577
00:45:16,409 --> 00:45:17,730
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, even that is your thoughts.

578
00:45:17,750 --> 00:45:24,374
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can't even intelligibly say whatever you're thinking, it's in my head, because that's in my head, which is in my head, which is in my head, which is in my head.

579
00:45:25,355 --> 00:45:25,915
[SPEAKER_00]: Indefinitely.

580
00:45:26,996 --> 00:45:35,242
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you realize, the notion of my head is because it's underlined by the four great elements.

581
00:45:36,043 --> 00:45:40,326
[SPEAKER_00]: There are also other notions, but the notion does not conceive

582
00:45:41,222 --> 00:45:50,810
[SPEAKER_00]: ...itself to be the actual four great elements, or to be apart from them, which would imply them to be something else, or to be in them, or to be from them, or to be for me, or to be among.

583
00:45:52,651 --> 00:45:54,493
[SPEAKER_00]: The notion just doesn't conceive any of that.

584
00:45:55,253 --> 00:45:58,576
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just the notion for... it's known... a notion is known as a notion.

585
00:45:59,817 --> 00:46:02,339
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it doesn't conceive that because of which the notion is.

586
00:46:07,148 --> 00:46:11,230
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, put it in more simpler terms, the notion is fully disowned.

587
00:46:12,171 --> 00:46:14,812
[SPEAKER_00]: The notion is discerned as impossible to own.

588
00:46:15,192 --> 00:46:16,113
[SPEAKER_00]: Notion is a dhamma.

589
00:46:17,073 --> 00:46:18,374
[SPEAKER_00]: A dhamma.

590
00:46:18,414 --> 00:46:19,315
[SPEAKER_00]: Notion is a phenomenon.

591
00:46:20,375 --> 00:46:26,919
[SPEAKER_00]: Notion of this, notion of that, thing, a thought, you can call it whatever you want, basically a phenomenon.

592
00:46:27,579 --> 00:46:29,620
[SPEAKER_00]: Phenomenon is that which has a nature to appear.

593
00:46:30,160 --> 00:46:31,061
[SPEAKER_00]: What has a nature to appear?

594
00:46:31,181 --> 00:46:32,922
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything has a nature to appear that you can talk about.

595
00:46:33,893 --> 00:46:37,054
[SPEAKER_00]: Things that have no need to appear, you can't possibly discern.

596
00:46:38,214 --> 00:46:40,214
[SPEAKER_00]: Since they don't appear, you can't even think about it.

597
00:46:43,955 --> 00:46:53,197
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, when you reach that understanding, abide in that understanding.

598
00:46:54,657 --> 00:46:55,077
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

599
00:46:56,578 --> 00:46:57,638
[SPEAKER_01]: Become that understanding.

600
00:46:58,553 --> 00:46:58,893
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

601
00:46:59,173 --> 00:47:02,935
[SPEAKER_01]: What you're saying about finding the balance in, you know, finding the balance in that.

602
00:47:03,575 --> 00:47:06,556
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you... Well, you don't need to balance it.

603
00:47:06,636 --> 00:47:08,877
[SPEAKER_00]: Once you understood, you can't undo the understanding.

604
00:47:09,177 --> 00:47:12,438
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's no balance to be maintained, because you're... it's developed.

605
00:47:13,238 --> 00:47:14,639
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why you know it's developed.

606
00:47:15,219 --> 00:47:17,100
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, the vision that you see, you see it.

607
00:47:17,680 --> 00:47:18,620
[SPEAKER_01]: What you're talking about now.

608
00:47:18,720 --> 00:47:19,260
[SPEAKER_01]: You see it.

609
00:47:19,520 --> 00:47:19,780
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

610
00:47:20,641 --> 00:47:26,983
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, you can... Well, you can know that it hasn't been developed sufficiently, or hasn't been developed fully.

611
00:47:27,792 --> 00:47:29,873
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you just have to keep repeating it and drilling it.

612
00:47:31,774 --> 00:47:33,035
[SPEAKER_00]: The very same inside.

613
00:47:43,021 --> 00:47:47,604
[SPEAKER_01]: By investigating those dhammas, those... Yeah.

614
00:47:48,664 --> 00:47:51,046
[SPEAKER_00]: By understanding the dhammas.

615
00:47:51,506 --> 00:47:55,969
[SPEAKER_00]: By understanding that which has a nature to appear, which is your thoughts, your feelings,

616
00:47:57,498 --> 00:47:58,258
[SPEAKER_00]: Your intentions.

617
00:48:04,420 --> 00:48:06,201
[SPEAKER_00]: Your perception has an age to appear.

618
00:48:07,081 --> 00:48:08,401
[SPEAKER_00]: Feeling has an age to appear.

619
00:48:08,722 --> 00:48:10,042
[SPEAKER_00]: Attention has an age to appear.

620
00:48:14,643 --> 00:48:18,745
[SPEAKER_00]: Even your attention has an age to appear.

621
00:48:18,765 --> 00:48:20,765
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you can talk about, I'm attending to this.

622
00:48:20,885 --> 00:48:26,007
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's indirect, it's negative in regard to what is being attended, but it appears.

623
00:48:26,922 --> 00:48:27,682
[SPEAKER_00]: There's a tension.

624
00:48:29,003 --> 00:48:30,403
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, all of that is nāma.

625
00:48:32,924 --> 00:48:33,704
[SPEAKER_00]: The designation.

626
00:48:34,564 --> 00:48:34,884
[SPEAKER_00]: Name.

627
00:48:37,525 --> 00:48:38,765
[SPEAKER_00]: And I said nāmarūpa.

628
00:48:39,986 --> 00:48:40,466
[SPEAKER_00]: The rūpa.

629
00:48:41,006 --> 00:48:41,446
[SPEAKER_00]: There you go.

630
00:48:41,686 --> 00:48:44,447
[SPEAKER_00]: You just said it in the same sense you said, in the same way you said nāma.

631
00:48:44,987 --> 00:48:46,547
[SPEAKER_00]: So rūpa is also designation.

632
00:48:49,728 --> 00:48:53,029
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's a more general designation than the designation of nāma.

633
00:48:53,989 --> 00:48:54,690
[SPEAKER_00]: More fundamental.

634
00:48:55,250 --> 00:48:55,750
[SPEAKER_00]: Direction.

635
00:48:56,841 --> 00:48:59,562
[SPEAKER_00]: But it still pertains actually to the nature of desimation.

636
00:49:00,362 --> 00:49:03,883
[SPEAKER_00]: That then stops conceiving itself to be that rūpa.

637
00:49:07,605 --> 00:49:08,105
[SPEAKER_00]: Nāmarūpa.

638
00:49:10,486 --> 00:49:11,086
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all.

639
00:49:12,126 --> 00:49:12,686
[SPEAKER_00]: What is all?

640
00:49:12,766 --> 00:49:13,327
[SPEAKER_00]: It's nāmarūpa.

641
00:49:13,407 --> 00:49:14,367
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all that can appear.

642
00:49:14,427 --> 00:49:16,128
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing else except nāmarūpa can appear.

643
00:49:20,849 --> 00:49:22,990
[SPEAKER_00]: But that doesn't mean that rūpa is actually

644
00:49:24,293 --> 00:49:28,797
[SPEAKER_00]: The rūpa, because of which nāmarūpa is as appearance.

645
00:49:34,703 --> 00:49:40,788
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's only one way to correctly, accurately designate rūpa.

646
00:49:41,989 --> 00:49:47,054
[SPEAKER_00]: And that way is by not having that designation stand for that rūpa.

647
00:49:48,620 --> 00:49:58,964
[SPEAKER_00]: If it doesn't, if it doesn't conceive that rūpa, the designation of rūpa doesn't conceive rūpa, that's the only accurate designation.

648
00:49:59,844 --> 00:50:00,925
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's liberation.

649
00:50:01,585 --> 00:50:14,510
[SPEAKER_00]: You practice that and it will be free from all conceivings, from all implications of mind, thus from all implications of I am, thus from all implications of self, myself and personality.

650
00:50:25,002 --> 00:50:36,111
[SPEAKER_00]: Or you can take your experience as a whole and regard... and you have kind of things... aspects of it that are more mental and aspects of it that are more material, so to speak.

651
00:50:36,972 --> 00:50:39,574
[SPEAKER_00]: But both are actually part of the designation.

652
00:50:39,774 --> 00:50:41,856
[SPEAKER_00]: nāma in regard to rūpa.

653
00:50:41,876 --> 00:50:45,879
[SPEAKER_00]: So what you have to do is that while they're simultaneously present,

654
00:50:47,561 --> 00:50:57,929
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, stop regarding the material aspect as... stop assuming the material aspect as pertaining to the actual method because of which the designation of material aspects can arise.

655
00:50:59,811 --> 00:51:00,812
[SPEAKER_00]: Stop conceiving them.

656
00:51:05,776 --> 00:51:13,482
[SPEAKER_00]: Because any movement of your mind, it's already pertaining to the... it appears.

657
00:51:13,742 --> 00:51:14,923
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, it's part and element.

658
00:51:16,064 --> 00:51:16,965
[SPEAKER_00]: In regard to rūpa,

659
00:51:19,705 --> 00:51:28,791
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can know your experience as a whole, in whatever shape and form can arise, is because of the four great elements.

660
00:51:31,353 --> 00:51:34,235
[SPEAKER_00]: As long as there's knowledge, well, then it won't be knowledge.

661
00:51:34,495 --> 00:51:35,496
[SPEAKER_00]: But as long as there's thought,

662
00:51:36,715 --> 00:51:40,117
[SPEAKER_00]: Does not conceive the four great elements through the thought about them.

663
00:51:40,618 --> 00:51:46,502
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't actually assume that that's what they are, or that there's something else, or elsewhere, or both, or neither.

664
00:51:47,303 --> 00:51:49,124
[SPEAKER_00]: You just don't give in to any of those.

665
00:51:49,144 --> 00:51:52,707
[SPEAKER_00]: You just have a thought of four great elements, so you don't overdo it, you don't underdo it.

666
00:51:56,549 --> 00:51:58,551
[SPEAKER_00]: And then that thought won't be conceiving that.

667
00:52:00,492 --> 00:52:04,195
[SPEAKER_00]: They won't find a footing in your experience, which means your experience will be free.

668
00:52:05,988 --> 00:52:10,091
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's just something that needs to be repeated on and on and on, through different means.

669
00:52:10,532 --> 00:52:23,582
[SPEAKER_00]: But you end up repeating the same principle, the right order of things.

670
00:52:23,602 --> 00:52:27,064
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I call it contemplationism.

671
00:52:27,284 --> 00:52:29,566
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a bit of a head-spinner.

672
00:52:29,606 --> 00:52:35,631
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's a head-spinner, if obviously you wanna be as particular as that.

673
00:52:37,431 --> 00:52:51,914
[SPEAKER_00]: But you don't have to, because there are much less particular things, sorry, much less ambiguous things that you can contemplate, that would be maintaining and obviously drilling the same principle.

674
00:52:52,574 --> 00:52:52,834
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

675
00:52:53,334 --> 00:52:55,355
[SPEAKER_00]: Not mine, not for me, not in my control.

676
00:52:57,835 --> 00:53:05,377
[SPEAKER_00]: If you extend that principle to the point of pertaining to the thought of not mine, not for me, not my control, then you won't leave anything excluded.

677
00:53:06,287 --> 00:53:11,389
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you repeat that long enough, then that thing will become apparent, because it does correspond with how things actually are.

678
00:53:11,750 --> 00:53:14,011
[SPEAKER_00]: Not yours, not for you, not in your control.

679
00:53:15,271 --> 00:53:15,872
[SPEAKER_00]: Where do you call it?

680
00:53:16,732 --> 00:53:17,012
[SPEAKER_01]: Outlet.

681
00:53:20,974 --> 00:53:22,535
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the Mūla Pāryāya Sutta.

682
00:53:22,555 --> 00:53:25,516
[SPEAKER_00]: The monks did not rejoice in the Buddha, because they didn't understand it.

683
00:53:37,914 --> 00:53:45,399
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, for example, there's elements that we're talking about today as well.

684
00:53:45,479 --> 00:53:51,384
[SPEAKER_01]: Sensual pleasure, I mean, the sensual pleasure element and renunciation element.

685
00:53:54,185 --> 00:53:57,768
[SPEAKER_01]: And the ill-will element and non-ill-will element.

686
00:53:59,049 --> 00:54:01,811
[SPEAKER_01]: Cruelty element and non-cruelty element.

687
00:54:04,333 --> 00:54:07,535
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when one is experiencing ill-will,

688
00:54:10,520 --> 00:54:12,081
[SPEAKER_01]: Non-ill will is the great.

689
00:54:13,122 --> 00:54:13,362
[SPEAKER_00]: Hmm.

690
00:54:15,884 --> 00:54:19,466
[SPEAKER_00]: And seeing those two things... Why is the non-ill will great?

691
00:54:20,487 --> 00:54:20,987
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is it?

692
00:54:28,412 --> 00:54:29,133
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is it more?

693
00:54:29,213 --> 00:54:29,973
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is it great?

694
00:54:30,193 --> 00:54:30,814
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is it great?

695
00:54:34,856 --> 00:54:36,698
[SPEAKER_01]: But it takes... doesn't take you.

696
00:54:36,878 --> 00:54:40,100
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, no, that's why... why... why it's wholesome.

697
00:54:42,358 --> 00:54:43,038
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is it greater?

698
00:54:43,759 --> 00:54:46,920
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is it structurally greater than ill-will?

699
00:54:47,200 --> 00:54:49,240
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is ill-will lower than non-ill-will?

700
00:54:51,781 --> 00:54:56,303
[SPEAKER_01]: Because ill-will is determined.

701
00:54:57,143 --> 00:55:03,285
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's because ill-will can only arise in regard to particular things.

702
00:55:03,305 --> 00:55:07,126
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I was trying to say.

703
00:55:07,186 --> 00:55:09,567
[SPEAKER_00]: If you experience ill-will, it's only in regard to something.

704
00:55:09,960 --> 00:55:15,545
[SPEAKER_00]: Even if it's a very general, ambiguous mood or thought, you're having ill-will in regard to that.

705
00:55:16,746 --> 00:55:19,608
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means, ill-will is always circumstantial.

706
00:55:20,229 --> 00:55:22,290
[SPEAKER_00]: Because these things could have not arisen.

707
00:55:24,192 --> 00:55:25,053
[SPEAKER_00]: But which is more?

708
00:55:25,733 --> 00:55:26,434
[SPEAKER_00]: Things that...

709
00:55:26,454 --> 00:55:27,595
[SPEAKER_00]: Sorry, you don't know which is more?

710
00:55:27,895 --> 00:55:28,976
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah.

711
00:55:28,996 --> 00:55:29,056
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

712
00:55:29,156 --> 00:55:33,920
[SPEAKER_00]: Can you have desire and lust or ill-will in regard to things that you've never seen, you've never heard, you've never thought of?

713
00:55:35,195 --> 00:55:35,635
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't.

714
00:55:35,896 --> 00:55:36,496
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't have it.

715
00:55:36,576 --> 00:55:45,403
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just... it's inconceivable to experience desire and lust or aversion in regard to that which is never... has never manifested in any particular form.

716
00:55:46,163 --> 00:55:48,305
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't have those... those things.

717
00:55:48,325 --> 00:55:50,167
[SPEAKER_00]: You can only have non-ill-will.

718
00:55:50,407 --> 00:55:53,429
[SPEAKER_00]: You can only have non-aversion, non-lust.

719
00:55:56,131 --> 00:55:57,252
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the default mode.

720
00:55:58,759 --> 00:56:03,360
[SPEAKER_00]: On a basis of non-lust, you develop lust in regard to something that's being manifested.

721
00:56:03,780 --> 00:56:11,121
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you know that I can't have lust in regard to things that are not manifested, that means that whatever is manifested, it's circumstantial.

722
00:56:12,881 --> 00:56:20,123
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if it was manifested, and has it been manifested before, if it was manifested, means it could have not been manifested.

723
00:56:20,583 --> 00:56:25,084
[SPEAKER_00]: And it certainly means, oh, it's manifested, thus it will unmanifest.

724
00:56:25,984 --> 00:56:27,524
[SPEAKER_00]: It will cease, because it has arisen.

725
00:56:30,123 --> 00:56:32,564
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't possibly have lust for that which doesn't manifest.

726
00:56:32,724 --> 00:56:35,245
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't possibly have real will for that which doesn't manifest.

727
00:56:37,867 --> 00:56:42,889
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, when you do have lust or real will, you recognize, oh, it's in regard to a circumstantial thing that could have not been.

728
00:56:44,170 --> 00:56:45,350
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, it's completely treacherous.

729
00:56:45,370 --> 00:56:47,031
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, it's unnecessary.

730
00:56:47,992 --> 00:56:49,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, it's impossible.

731
00:56:50,953 --> 00:56:52,474
[SPEAKER_00]: Because lust would actually imply

732
00:56:54,640 --> 00:56:59,703
[SPEAKER_00]: That whole notion of, oh, this is special, this is particular, this is worthy, this is valuable, this is great.

733
00:57:00,623 --> 00:57:04,986
[SPEAKER_00]: But when you recognize that it's circumstantial, it, it, it, it, well, it loses its elevated state.

734
00:57:05,026 --> 00:57:05,786
[SPEAKER_00]: This is important.

735
00:57:05,926 --> 00:57:06,787
[SPEAKER_00]: This is important, yeah.

736
00:57:07,167 --> 00:57:10,469
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what it means by saying that non-ill will is greater.

737
00:57:11,409 --> 00:57:12,410
[SPEAKER_00]: It's more fundamental.

738
00:57:13,490 --> 00:57:14,351
[SPEAKER_00]: It's more important.

739
00:57:17,332 --> 00:57:17,612
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

740
00:57:17,813 --> 00:57:22,215
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there are more things that have been arisen

741
00:57:23,769 --> 00:57:25,390
[SPEAKER_00]: There are more things that are manifested.

742
00:57:26,591 --> 00:57:28,932
[SPEAKER_00]: And for them, which you can't have... for them, you can't have lust.

743
00:57:29,013 --> 00:57:31,654
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't have ill will, which means there is more non-ill will.

744
00:57:32,015 --> 00:57:33,355
[SPEAKER_00]: Even for people who are always angry.

745
00:57:33,816 --> 00:57:38,359
[SPEAKER_00]: They're always angry at something particular, which means, on the general level, there is more non-ill will.

746
00:57:39,399 --> 00:57:42,141
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why you don't do the non-ill will.

747
00:57:42,562 --> 00:57:43,462
[SPEAKER_00]: You just discern it.

748
00:57:44,143 --> 00:57:46,244
[SPEAKER_00]: And because of that, you can't engage in ill will.

749
00:57:47,565 --> 00:57:49,006
[SPEAKER_00]: And same, you discern that

750
00:57:49,728 --> 00:57:54,750
[SPEAKER_00]: Absence of passion has an inherent characteristics of the five aggregates.

751
00:57:55,851 --> 00:57:59,452
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of that, you stop at the ten notions of passion in regard to the five aggregates.

752
00:58:01,453 --> 00:58:02,934
[SPEAKER_00]: Upādāna is not the five aggregates.

753
00:58:03,594 --> 00:58:04,634
[SPEAKER_00]: It can't possibly be.

754
00:58:06,175 --> 00:58:08,496
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not found anywhere else apart from them.

755
00:58:09,036 --> 00:58:13,378
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the desire and lust in regard to five aggregates that the assumption is there.

756
00:58:22,610 --> 00:58:33,514
[SPEAKER_00]: It's greater than particular manifestation of desire and lust in regard to the particular manifestation of the five aggregates.

757
00:58:35,094 --> 00:58:36,475
[SPEAKER_00]: It's always circumstantial.

758
00:58:36,535 --> 00:58:37,735
[SPEAKER_00]: It always could have not been.

759
00:58:38,436 --> 00:58:40,136
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's another the contemplation is called before.

760
00:58:40,496 --> 00:58:43,337
[SPEAKER_00]: You start thinking that over the things that are appearing.

761
00:58:43,897 --> 00:58:48,079
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, this could have not been and it will... this it will... it will... it will not be for me.

762
00:58:50,017 --> 00:59:05,551
[SPEAKER_00]: So, things that will be, will not be for me, because that circumstantialness of it, the thread of it, just pertains to the past, to the present, and the past that is present, and the future that is present as a possibility.

763
00:59:06,312 --> 00:59:13,559
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, so when the things in the future, if this wall still remains standing, arise, it's impossible for them to arise for me.

764
00:59:15,141 --> 00:59:20,364
[SPEAKER_00]: As much as this present thing is also impossible to be accessed by me, it's possible to be for me.

765
00:59:21,224 --> 00:59:25,006
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, you realize, oh, my whole past was actually never for me and thus it was never mine.

766
00:59:29,468 --> 00:59:33,149
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's how you don't dwell in the past and you don't go in the future.

767
00:59:34,230 --> 00:59:41,893
[SPEAKER_00]: By descending the present, by descending then through the present, not by stopping your thinking and refraining from thinking about your past.

768
00:59:50,916 --> 00:59:59,202
[SPEAKER_00]: But by fully discerning that the thing is inaccessible now, that nature pertains in the future, and that nature pervades the past.

769
01:00:00,844 --> 01:00:07,208
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's why Arahant does not... like, you know, he was in Arahant always, but when he becomes in Arahant, he doesn't have thoughts anymore.

770
01:00:07,308 --> 01:00:08,169
[SPEAKER_00]: I was in the past.

771
01:00:08,549 --> 01:00:10,871
[SPEAKER_00]: Now I'm in Arahant, but I was in the past before.

772
01:00:11,231 --> 01:00:13,733
[SPEAKER_00]: I actually was as a person.

773
01:00:13,873 --> 01:00:14,394
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

774
01:00:14,554 --> 01:00:16,375
[SPEAKER_00]: That whole thing is affected.

775
01:00:17,436 --> 01:00:17,616
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

776
01:00:17,656 --> 01:00:18,437
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you're present.

777
01:00:24,778 --> 01:00:45,774
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, you don't have always laid in front of you past, present, future, because it will require an entity, a subject, that kind of has an overview over these three things, that are flowing in front of your eyes, as a as a slideshow or something.

778
01:00:46,534 --> 01:00:47,475
[SPEAKER_00]: You are part of that.

779
01:00:48,021 --> 01:00:56,384
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means you can only have over-determined present, that is present, or under-determined present, that is present.

780
01:00:57,405 --> 01:01:06,748
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, you can have past, that is present, if that's the direction you're looking, or if you look in the direction of possibilities, you can have the future, that is not yet present, and that's present.

781
01:01:08,309 --> 01:01:09,449
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's a bit more complex.

782
01:01:10,010 --> 01:01:12,731
[SPEAKER_00]: Complex for people who commonly think, eh...

783
01:01:13,531 --> 01:01:15,472
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't think about the future, don't worry about the past.

784
01:01:15,772 --> 01:01:16,092
[SPEAKER_01]: Why not?

785
01:01:17,080 --> 01:01:19,361
[SPEAKER_00]: That's present and you have no choice about that present.

786
01:01:21,983 --> 01:01:24,225
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, don't don't regard your past as yours.

787
01:01:25,205 --> 01:01:29,088
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't plan your future as belonging to you, as pertaining to you, as arising for you.

788
01:01:30,048 --> 01:01:30,809
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no problem.

789
01:01:31,189 --> 01:01:32,390
[SPEAKER_00]: You can know the future you want.

790
01:01:40,435 --> 01:01:41,075
[SPEAKER_00]: It might not be.

791
01:01:41,095 --> 01:01:41,656
[SPEAKER_00]: It might not be.

792
01:01:41,856 --> 01:01:42,116
[SPEAKER_00]: Sorry.

793
01:01:42,176 --> 01:01:42,696
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be.

794
01:01:42,716 --> 01:01:43,517
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be for me.

795
01:01:46,252 --> 01:01:48,074
[SPEAKER_00]: And certainly, it could have not been.

796
01:01:49,175 --> 01:01:51,557
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever it is, it could have been not.

797
01:01:54,019 --> 01:01:54,759
[SPEAKER_01]: Circumstantial.

798
01:01:54,959 --> 01:01:55,700
[SPEAKER_00]: Circumstantial.

799
01:02:00,764 --> 01:02:12,354
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you make any choices, any decisions, commit any acts, based on that which is circumstantial, you can only regard those choices, those acts as yours,

800
01:02:13,410 --> 01:02:30,298
[SPEAKER_00]: If you forget or if you don't fully discern the dependence of your choices upon this circumstantially arisen thing, if you remain mindful of the circumstantial nature of the arisen thing upon which you're acting and choosing and deciding, you won't be owning your choice either.

801
01:02:32,562 --> 01:02:34,203
[SPEAKER_00]: But that can be only when present.

802
01:02:34,684 --> 01:02:39,668
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't go in hindsight and say, ah, well, because things are not mine, my decisions are not mine as well.

803
01:02:40,229 --> 01:02:42,891
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's wishful thinking.

804
01:02:42,931 --> 01:02:44,112
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to see that directly.

805
01:02:45,013 --> 01:02:49,617
[SPEAKER_00]: While things are seen as not yours, what you're deciding upon that will not be yours.

806
01:02:50,117 --> 01:02:52,359
[SPEAKER_00]: And that limits the things you can decide.

807
01:02:53,300 --> 01:02:57,444
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if you do see circumstantially or reasoned things as present,

808
01:02:58,086 --> 01:03:05,951
[SPEAKER_00]: Simultaneously present determinations of your choices in regard to the circumstantial themes, your choices cannot be affected by lust, aversion and delusion.

809
01:03:10,994 --> 01:03:11,714
[SPEAKER_00]: It's impossible.

810
01:03:17,998 --> 01:03:21,080
[SPEAKER_00]: Because lust, aversion and delusion require that.

811
01:03:22,042 --> 01:03:24,263
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it requires the opposite of circumstantial.

812
01:03:24,563 --> 01:03:28,483
[SPEAKER_00]: It requires the special, the important, the mind.

813
01:03:32,664 --> 01:03:34,165
[SPEAKER_00]: But you see that it can't be yours.

814
01:03:34,625 --> 01:03:35,345
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not special.

815
01:03:35,905 --> 01:03:41,246
[SPEAKER_00]: It's particularly arisen on account of the basis of all of it that's not arisen.

816
01:03:42,507 --> 01:03:43,667
[SPEAKER_00]: And you can't have lust towards it.

817
01:03:43,727 --> 01:03:45,487
[SPEAKER_00]: And you certainly can't have ill will towards it.

818
01:03:46,848 --> 01:03:48,328
[SPEAKER_00]: And you won't be able to do anything about it.

819
01:03:52,431 --> 01:03:53,491
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just not worthy anymore.

820
01:03:54,371 --> 01:03:55,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

821
01:03:55,132 --> 01:03:55,932
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what Buddha said.

822
01:03:55,952 --> 01:04:00,293
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not worthy of delight, of craving.

823
01:04:01,793 --> 01:04:02,453
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not worthy.

824
01:04:05,214 --> 01:04:06,635
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you automatically stop doing it.

825
01:04:20,198 --> 01:04:20,438
[SPEAKER_01]: Even

826
01:04:23,403 --> 01:04:36,346
[SPEAKER_01]: The grief that arises through abandoning this... in this realm, again, grief that arises...

827
01:04:36,366 --> 01:04:37,466
[SPEAKER_00]: It's with... yeah, it's with embed.

828
01:04:38,347 --> 01:04:39,647
[SPEAKER_00]: Even that is circumstantial.

829
01:04:40,167 --> 01:04:42,968
[SPEAKER_00]: So you surround that... You surround grief as well, yeah.

830
01:04:45,088 --> 01:04:46,809
[SPEAKER_00]: Because grief is grief only when it's mine.

831
01:04:47,589 --> 01:04:52,550
[SPEAKER_00]: But... You stop grieving when it doesn't pertain to you anymore.

832
01:05:06,190 --> 01:05:12,472
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you're renouncing sensual pleasures, that's keeping restraint.

833
01:05:12,492 --> 01:05:16,734
[SPEAKER_00]: You're emulating the right order of things.

834
01:05:17,394 --> 01:05:31,820
[SPEAKER_01]: But you also know, no matter what happens because of your renouncing, because of your not engaging in sensual pleasures, it can't...

835
01:05:31,840 --> 01:05:32,640
[SPEAKER_00]: It'll be a good thing.

836
01:05:32,800 --> 01:05:33,541
[SPEAKER_01]: It'll be a good thing.

837
01:05:33,681 --> 01:05:33,901
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

838
01:05:34,101 --> 01:05:34,381
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's

839
01:05:36,111 --> 01:05:36,952
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's what Guruji said.

840
01:05:37,092 --> 01:05:56,304
[SPEAKER_00]: Even if a person doesn't develop any wisdom, even if a monk doesn't develop any wisdom, stays a pūtugina, basically, and lives his holy life, his renunciate life, in tears, because of the pain of restraining sensuality, it's still better than giving in to sensuality.

841
01:05:57,285 --> 01:06:00,367
[SPEAKER_00]: Because at least he's living the principle.

842
01:06:02,749 --> 01:06:04,130
[SPEAKER_00]: The principle of non-lust.

843
01:06:04,829 --> 01:06:07,871
[SPEAKER_01]: Because anyone can sort of... well, I wouldn't say anyone...

844
01:06:07,911 --> 01:06:17,158
[SPEAKER_00]: He won't be enlightened as a result of it, but he certainly, by living the principle, yeah, he brings himself closer to the enlightenment, obviously, in lives to come.

845
01:06:18,118 --> 01:06:19,679
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's still better in the long run.

846
01:06:21,441 --> 01:06:23,282
[SPEAKER_01]: But when you have the knowledge that...

847
01:06:23,322 --> 01:06:32,829
[SPEAKER_00]: When you have the knowledge that discerns the principle that you start living beforehand, which is why sīla has to come first, then the knowledge discerns, then you basically...

848
01:06:34,243 --> 01:06:34,663
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

849
01:06:35,084 --> 01:06:36,544
[SPEAKER_00]: You discern, you fully understood.

850
01:06:37,024 --> 01:06:39,805
[SPEAKER_00]: Now you don't even have to keep doing it, because you are it.

851
01:06:40,326 --> 01:06:43,327
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't have to keep emulating the principle, when you become a principle.

852
01:06:45,448 --> 01:06:46,368
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it takes over.

853
01:06:46,728 --> 01:06:47,689
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yes.

854
01:06:51,390 --> 01:06:53,811
[SPEAKER_00]: Otherwise, you can spend all emulating you want.

855
01:06:54,672 --> 01:06:59,273
[SPEAKER_00]: Nobody points out to you, if you don't discern it, you won't, you will remain a tutor.

856
01:07:00,574 --> 01:07:03,055
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's why there is no dhamma without sīla.

857
01:07:04,401 --> 01:07:05,942
[SPEAKER_00]: But certainly, sīla is not dhamma.

858
01:07:07,764 --> 01:07:12,628
[SPEAKER_00]: But dhamma is impossible to have without starting with emulation of the right principle.

859
01:07:15,610 --> 01:07:17,992
[SPEAKER_01]: Because dhamma doesn't properly renunciation.

860
01:07:19,453 --> 01:07:22,596
[SPEAKER_00]: It can very easily lead to wisdom, with very little instruction.

861
01:07:24,212 --> 01:07:28,193
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why he sees the danger in the slightest thought.

862
01:07:28,773 --> 01:07:32,174
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't mean he becomes neurotic, obsessed with anxiety.

863
01:07:32,834 --> 01:07:35,355
[SPEAKER_00]: It means he sees the danger, he starts discerning it.

864
01:07:35,975 --> 01:07:41,416
[SPEAKER_00]: The slightest deviation from the principle can be an obstacle, a massive obstacle later on.

865
01:07:41,616 --> 01:07:42,516
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a big danger.

866
01:07:42,636 --> 01:07:43,877
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I won't deviate.

867
01:07:46,657 --> 01:07:49,018
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, you know, your ship is on a course.

868
01:07:50,082 --> 01:07:55,247
[SPEAKER_00]: In your mind, more or less, it's just, just, just like, I don't know, 0.01 degree.

869
01:07:56,408 --> 01:08:03,875
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, if that course goes long enough, that 0.1 can cause you to miss the whole continent.

870
01:08:05,357 --> 01:08:06,798
[SPEAKER_00]: Because eventually, you pull that out.

871
01:08:23,410 --> 01:08:42,396
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you, if you literally, if you just start emulating the principle of non-lust, non-aversion, non-delusion, non-indolence, with your body, with your speech, and with your mind, with lethal instruction from the suttas, then more than enough.

872
01:08:42,756 --> 01:08:44,977
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, you need to emulate the principle harder.

873
01:08:45,457 --> 01:08:52,959
[SPEAKER_00]: With more discerned instructions, you can emulate it to a lesser extent, because then the knowledge can take root quicker.

874
01:08:53,305 --> 01:08:54,426
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, obviously, you become it.

875
01:08:55,367 --> 01:09:00,130
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't mean, like, somebody will keep the precepts less, if they understand.

876
01:09:00,270 --> 01:09:08,857
[SPEAKER_00]: On the contrary, they need to worry less about the precepts, when they understand, or if they have more understanding.

877
01:09:08,997 --> 01:09:10,118
[SPEAKER_00]: It will take the root quicker.

878
01:09:11,059 --> 01:09:22,007
[SPEAKER_00]: But for those who don't have, who have, like, lots of faith, and they just emulate heavily, they might... they really need to, like, like, take, you know, a whole new level of emulation, and then it will take root.

879
01:09:22,850 --> 01:09:24,711
[SPEAKER_00]: Even with a little knowledge, they might have.

880
01:09:25,952 --> 01:09:26,792
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, they need to have.

881
01:09:27,713 --> 01:09:33,837
[SPEAKER_00]: Without any knowledge, again, as I said, you can emulate the principle all you want, live a very wholesome life, become very authentic.

882
01:09:34,677 --> 01:09:36,919
[SPEAKER_00]: But you can still remain putujana if nobody points out.

883
01:09:36,939 --> 01:09:43,503
[SPEAKER_00]: But today, it's kind of impossible, because today, nobody emulates the principle of wholesome living.

884
01:09:44,383 --> 01:09:51,728
[SPEAKER_00]: And those who do, do it as a result of the Buddha's instruction, which means those who emulate the principle are already familiar enough with the Buddha's teaching.

885
01:09:55,007 --> 01:10:00,648
[SPEAKER_00]: They may not go into all the details that we just talked about, for example, conceiving and stuff, but they don't eat it.

886
01:10:01,728 --> 01:10:03,129
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it emulates...

887
01:10:03,169 --> 01:10:07,289
[SPEAKER_00]: It emulates the principle and then you start discerning that that is how things actually are.

888
01:10:08,090 --> 01:10:09,870
[SPEAKER_00]: Not yours, not for you, not in your control.

889
01:10:11,030 --> 01:10:13,351
[SPEAKER_00]: Not possible to actually be affected by lust.

890
01:10:13,691 --> 01:10:15,431
[SPEAKER_00]: Not possible to be affected by rage.

891
01:10:16,231 --> 01:10:20,092
[SPEAKER_00]: Not possible to be affected by delusion, ignorance.

892
01:10:23,836 --> 01:10:25,537
[SPEAKER_00]: And then all the factors will follow.

893
01:10:27,198 --> 01:10:33,601
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a slower process than the one who is emulating the principle and actively trying to understand it.

894
01:10:34,881 --> 01:10:35,182
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

895
01:10:35,202 --> 01:10:35,742
[SPEAKER_01]: It's doubled.

896
01:10:36,222 --> 01:10:36,482
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

897
01:10:36,882 --> 01:10:37,523
[SPEAKER_00]: Doubled.

898
01:10:37,623 --> 01:10:40,224
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, basically, you fight on both fronts.

899
01:10:48,096 --> 01:10:49,897
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's the same emulation, it's the same...

900
01:10:50,177 --> 01:10:52,099
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's the same result and it's the same emulation, yeah.

901
01:10:52,439 --> 01:10:52,819
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

902
01:10:52,839 --> 01:11:03,206
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just always if somebody's just emulating the principle, but not trying to understand the principle as well, then you might have people with greater intellectual capacities.

903
01:11:03,366 --> 01:11:06,588
[SPEAKER_00]: They can understand the principle with actually quite a pure emulation.

904
01:11:08,409 --> 01:11:08,549
[SPEAKER_00]: i.e.

905
01:11:08,649 --> 01:11:14,894
[SPEAKER_00]: their sīla is not actually developed properly, but they have quite some intelligence, they can discern, and then they'll develop.

906
01:11:15,174 --> 01:11:16,955
[SPEAKER_00]: But until they develop their sīla properly,

907
01:11:18,322 --> 01:11:21,323
[SPEAKER_00]: This understanding of that principle will not reach to fulfillment.

908
01:11:22,043 --> 01:11:38,770
[SPEAKER_00]: That way, sotāpannas, who have, who have sīla sufficiently for sotāpatti, but are not arahants yet, they need to keep practicing nekamā, renunciation, restraint, until the principle fully permeates everything.

909
01:11:39,230 --> 01:11:46,913
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they just need to stick to the virtuous living, sotāpannas, and they'll become arahants, because they fully understood the principle.

910
01:11:52,020 --> 01:11:58,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, the ones who didn't stick to the virtuous living, you know, they didn't compromise their understanding.

911
01:11:58,566 --> 01:11:59,987
[SPEAKER_00]: They just slowed down their progress.

912
01:12:00,788 --> 01:12:09,875
[SPEAKER_00]: Like the sotāpānas in the suttas that I mentioned, or in the vinaya rules, you know, the drinking, like lay people as well.

913
01:12:10,776 --> 01:12:13,218
[SPEAKER_00]: He was a sotāpāna, but he was drunk, and so on.

914
01:12:13,458 --> 01:12:14,859
[SPEAKER_01]: So he wasn't keeping the precepts.

915
01:12:17,361 --> 01:12:17,541
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

916
01:12:17,581 --> 01:12:20,764
[SPEAKER_00]: Because he had faculties developed.

917
01:12:21,401 --> 01:12:31,447
[SPEAKER_00]: Such an extent that he could discern the principle at the very little occasion where he did keep the principle, where he did live awesomely, and he discerned the principle.

918
01:12:32,367 --> 01:12:36,370
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you know, his habit and lust took him over, but the principle was discerned.

919
01:12:36,870 --> 01:12:39,812
[SPEAKER_00]: So, at most, in seven lifetimes, he would have brought the fulfillment.

920
01:12:41,573 --> 01:12:44,995
[SPEAKER_00]: And there's a thing that says when he's discerning the principle, he's virtuous.

921
01:12:46,359 --> 01:12:52,021
[SPEAKER_00]: So, at the moment of death, when you can't engage in anything circumstantial, he is that principle.

922
01:13:02,506 --> 01:13:05,227
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why it's often... it's such a prominent

923
01:13:06,741 --> 01:13:18,583
[SPEAKER_00]: There's kind of a role of that in the sutra, when somebody who has the right view, or who is... who's already reached the... oh, well, he might attain... if he doesn't attain the fruits of his understanding in this life, he will attain the moment of death.

924
01:13:20,663 --> 01:13:21,303
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

925
01:13:22,684 --> 01:13:23,844
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's where the principle is.

926
01:13:25,024 --> 01:13:26,844
[SPEAKER_00]: Not mine, not for me, not in my control.

